---
// What the county must do (decision #118): the Constitution's Fourth Schedule, Part 2, in plain words. Place pages
// cite its items in "Who is responsible". The items are summaries for finding your way; the official text governs.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import C from '../../data/constitution.json';
const F = C.fourthSchedule;
---
<Base title="How Nyamira County is governed" description="The county government's functions under Kenya's Constitution (Fourth Schedule, Part 2), in plain words.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="The county" title="What the county must do" lead={F.summary} crumbs={[{ href: '/map/', label: 'Places' }, { href: '/administration/duties/', label: 'What the county must do' }]} />
  <div class="stack" style="margin-top:16px; max-width:760px">
    <p>When a place page says who is responsible for a clinic, a market or a road, it points to an item on this list. If a service is not on it, it is usually the national government's job: for example primary and secondary schools, and national roads.</p>
    <ol class="rows" style="list-style:none">
      {F.functions.map((f) => (
        <li id={`item-${f.n}`} style="padding:12px 4px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)">
          <span class="t"><strong>{f.n}. {f.title}</strong></span>
          <span class="d" style="display:block; color:var(--muted)">{f.covers}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <p class="small muted">These are short summaries to help you find your way, not the legal text. Read the official text in <a href={C.officialUrl} rel="noopener">the Constitution of Kenya, 2010</a> (Fourth Schedule, Part 2). Something wrong? <a href="/about/rules/#corrections">Tell us</a>.</p>

    <!-- Kiswahili: needs native-speaker review -->
    <div class="sw" lang="sw"><span class="eyebrow">Muhtasari kwa Kiswahili</span><p>Majukumu ya serikali ya kaunti kama yalivyoainishwa katika Katiba ya Kenya (Ratiba ya Nne, Sehemu ya 2) — afya, elimu, barabara, maji, kilimo na mengineyo.</p></div>
  </div>
</Base>
